ID: B2-Ch07a-Intro
TEXT:

 

"Barry, how long are you going to glare at that scrap of paper?" Daren leans against the stall post, crossing his arms. "I told you. My wards do not conflict. You cannot find what is not there."

I keep my eyes on the parchment spread between my boots, pencil tapping against the margins of my notebook. The sheet lists every ward Daren layers onto himself before a fight, cross-referenced against my own handwritten diagrams of eastern white-magic theory. Most of the formulas match, but the loophole Eiden used to drop Daren into slumber still eludes me. Beside me, Hadrik sits cross-legged in the dirt, chin in his hand, squinting at the ink and tossing out wild theories with all the authority of a giant who has never cast a white-magic spell in his life.

Flower peeked over my shoulder twice, announced that the tiny script made her forehead throb, and wandered off toward a fruit stall. Illuna made her position clear from the start: elven spirit or not, human warding structures are outside her interest, and she refuses to waste breath on guesses.

"Here," Hadrik rumbles, jabbing a thick finger at a line near the bottom. "The cadence on this illusion ward sounds almost identical to the sleep ward next to it. What if the resonance clashes?"

"Phonetics don't dictate harmonic clashes," I tell him. "Dozens of standard incantations share phonetic roots without collapsing. It's something structural. Something obvious right in front of me. I'm going back to the first line."

"Gods above, Barry," Daren groans, throwing his hands up. "Did it ever occur to you that Eiden was toying with you? Why would he hand you the flaw in his own spellwork? What reason could he possibly have?"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Intro2, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Intro2, v_checkpoint_rich = 0)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Intro2
TEXT:

 "Aren't you the one who volunteered your greatest vulnerability five minutes after we shook hands?" I ask, looking up from the page.

"That is entirely different!" Daren snaps. "Any veteran swordsman would deduce that my barrier struggles against enchanted steel after watching me fight for two rounds!"

"Wait, you struggle against enchanted weapons?" Hadrik asks, blinking.

Daren lets out a low, pained groan.

"No, truly," Hadrik rumbles, leaning forward. "I never caught that. Why enchanted steel specifically? Shouldn't a standard shield weave turn aside most blows? Are you cursed? And why rely on a basic shield at all? Beginner casters lean on shields because they lack control, but the weave bleeds energy and barely softens a killing blow. Dedicated protection matrices against blunt impact or piercing force work far better. Not that I ever bothered studying warding geometry, what with giant hide turning aside iron on its own."

"White mages use advanced variations of the shield weave," Daren says, stiffening. "They are vastly more efficient. And the flaw is not confined to enchanted steel. My aura resists physical trauma protections across the board. Remember the ogre captain hurling me into the fortress wall with his club? I have tested dozens of physical protection formulas, but none take hold in my aura. The advanced shield weave is the sole construct that offers even marginal defense against physical impacts, and it barely holds against mundane steel, let alone enchanted blades. Enchanting my plate armor to maximum durability was the only way I found to survive on the battlefield."

"Huh," Hadrik muses, scratching his beard. "Strange. Do you suppose it connects to the spirit on the magical plane Arraka mentioned? Like your spirit has some aversion to earthen matter? Barry, what's your read?"

choice(""I'd say that's certainly a possibility."", B2-Ch07a-Possibility, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Possibility)
choice(""I'd be more inclined to think that he linked himself to the spirit incorrectly."", B2-Ch07a-Incorrectly, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Incorrectly)
choice(""I don't think it's related. He probably just got born this way."", B2-Ch07a-Related, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Related)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Possibility
TEXT:

 "I'd say that's certainly a possibility."

"Well," Daren mutters, rubbing his scarred temple, "if it turns out I have spent fifteen years compensating with plate armor because some otherworldly spirit has an aversion to dirt, I will be thoroughly furious. I am better off in ignorance."

"The armor serves you better than a shield weave in most melees anyway," I say, running a finger down the column. "It costs no aura to maintain, and you don't have to balance it against your other—wait. Did you just say you are running an advanced shield weave right now?"

"Of course," Daren says. "It is the only spell in my repertoire that blunts physical blows. I would be a fool to leave it down."

"Then why isn't it on this parchment?!" I demand, tapping the graphite against the sheet. "Didn't I tell you to record every defensive enchantment active on our second day on the island, without exception?"

"I told you on our first morning that I keep a shield weave active," Daren says. "And why would it matter? What does a physical shield construct have to do with conflicting sleep wards?"

"It has everything to do with them!" I say. "Have you never cracked a single volume of Azarius's 'Advanced Theory of Magic'?"

"Some of us did not spend our youth buried in academy archives," Daren shoots back. "Everything I know of the craft was passed down by master enchanters."

"Then your masters skipped foundational harmonics!" I tell him.

"You take that back!" Daren bristles. "My white-magic mentor was an ex-sage! Do you have any conception of the mastery required to claim a sage title through white magic alone, without a scrap of combat casting?"

"Not enough to teach harmonic resonance, apparently," I say.

"Gods above!" Daren raises his hands. "Do you possess no respect whatsoever for the discipline it takes to—"

"What is happening here?" Kate asks, stepping into the shade of the stall with Leila at her side, bundles of linen and leather in hand. "What are you two arguing about now?"

"Barry refuses to acknowledge the mastery required to—" Daren begins, but I cut across him.

"Never mind that! Daren, which shield weave are you using? Is it the third-edition matrix tailored against physical impact?"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Overload, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Overload)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Incorrectly
TEXT:

 "I'd be more inclined to think that he linked himself to the spirit incorrectly."

"Easy to say from the ground," Daren says, crossing his arms. "You aren't a caster. Every spark of magic you have channeled came through that mechanical booster. Even with Arraka's lecture in mind, I have no idea how to perceive that bridge to the magical plane. I have examined my aura currents for hours and found no distinct conduit."

"The armor serves you better than a shield weave in most melees anyway," I say, running a finger down the column. "It costs no aura to maintain, and you don't have to balance it against your other—wait. Did you just say you are running an advanced shield weave right now?"

