ID: B2-Ch07a-Related
TEXT:

 "I don't think it's related. He probably just got born this way."

"Realistically, Barry is right," Daren says, letting his hands fall. "I am all for blaming an unseen ethereal entity across the planes, but the truth is simpler. I accepted years ago that my aura rejects physical warding. It doesn't trouble me as it once did."

"The armor serves you better than a shield weave in most melees anyway," I say, running a finger down the column. "It costs no aura to maintain, and you don't have to balance it against your other—wait. Did you just say you are running an advanced shield weave right now?"

