"Hah!" Arraka's muffled laugh echoes from the golden casing. "Now that is a spectacle I'd pay to watch: Eiden undone by his own parlor tricks."

"Let's not get ahead of ourselves," Daren cautions. "Barry deduced two mechanical flaws. A six-century stillwater likely commands hundreds. But we have reached the palace gates. Let's finish our business with the crown."

We pass through the outer portcullis into the palace courtyard. The king's servant waits at the entrance, bowing respectfully before leading us into the throne room. Golmyck is on his knees behind the dais, spanner in hand, adjusting the bronze pneumatic pistons beneath the throne.

