#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1 && v_b2_ch2_deal != 3) {
 "Very well, then," Golmyck says. "Let me just finish stamping these documents, and you'll be free to go."

He stamps two more documents and hands them over for us to review.

"There you go," the king says. "These papers should be enough to absolve you of your crimes, no matter where you go in Varathia. Now, if there's nothing else you need from me, I will be resuming my work on the lessathi device that was supposed to send you the instructions related to the tournament's objectives, telepathically. I've been trying to get it fixed for more than a week, but I still can't figure out what's wrong with it, so you can imagine how frustrating this has been for me."

The king wishes us safe travels, and we head back up to the throne room, where the servant waits.

After he leads us outside, it takes about an hour and a half to reach the mansion, where Rose is still busy preparing our feast.

}
 With plenty of time left before the meal, Hadrik pulls a deck of cards from his backpack, and we sit down at a picnic table in the courtyard for a game he learned in dwarven taverns. The original rules called for a swig of dwarven ale on every lost hand, but we scrap that rule to avoid being drunk before dinner.

The game relies heavily on bluffing, so Leila dominates the table with her aura-reading. Since my spiky aura makes me the easiest read of all, I tire of losing every round and step away to consult my notebook, hoping to unravel more of Eiden's techniques.

"Hey, Daren," I say after reviewing my notes. "Remember when Eiden paralyzed everyone right before teleporting us to Thilias?"

"What?..." Daren tries to balance his cards while answering. "Oh, yeah. What about it?"

"How many paralysis wards were you using?"

"Just one," Daren says. "And the shield has no paralysis component, so it wasn't protection overload!"

"Alright," I say. "Is anyone else using paralysis wards?"

"Yes," Kate says. "I use the formula from Azarius's latest treatise."

"Alright," I say. "And you, Daren? Which ward?"

"The golden one," Daren says. "The spinning sparkle matrix."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-No-Help2, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-No-Help2)


ID: B2-Ch07a-No-Help2
TEXT:

 "So the standard white-mage volume," I say. "And Hadrik, you rely on natural giant resistance to shrug off such spells?"

"Yeah," Hadrik says. "Yet I froze solid alongside Kate and Daren."

"And do you know what those three defenses share?" I close the notebook. "Nothing. Which means Eiden wasn't exploiting a loophole. He wasn't casting paralysis at all. Remember when Kate's friend knocked us flat? That wasn't sleep magic. It was lightning. Eiden used an electric current to lock your muscles. You felt an initial jolt before falling, followed by periodic shocks to keep you immobilized."

"Now that you mention it, yes," Daren says. "I did feel periodic shocks. The sensation felt so similar to paralysis that I didn't question it. Does that mean Eiden wields lightning as an element?"

"Doubtful," I say. "The spell had rigid constraints that wouldn't apply to freeform elemental lightning. It matches an ability from my stat device, so it's likely identical. It carries a once-a-day limit and a very narrow radius. Rolling a couple feet to the side puts you out of range. It worked because you stood close together and didn't recognize the construct. If you know the timing, you can roll clear right before the next pulse hits, as the paralysis weakens briefly between discharges."

"Easier said than done," Daren mutters. "I was fighting the effect the entire time."

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
 "Straining against it only triggers faster pulses!" I say. "You have to stay relaxed and move at the final second. You track the rhythm over a couple shocks, find the pattern, and roll when the window opens. A dedicated lightning ward avoids the problem entirely, though keeping one active around the clock drains far too much energy."

"Not to cut this short," Hadrik says, "but we should finish the round before Enrique finishes cooking. We have maybe twenty minutes left, and everyone except Leila is holding at least five cards."

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
 "Straining against it only triggers faster pulses!" I say. "You have to stay relaxed and move at the final second. You track the rhythm over a couple shocks, find the pattern, and roll when the window opens. A dedicated lightning ward avoids the problem entirely, though keeping one active around the clock drains far too much energy."

"Not to cut this short," Hadrik says, "but we should finish the round before Rose finishes cooking. We have maybe twenty minutes left, and everyone except Leila is holding at least five cards."

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Mansion2, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Mansion2)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Help
TEXT:

 "Now, then..." Golmyck's gaze turns serious. "Leaving Eiden and the calamity aside, we have a more pressing matter to resolve. Are you still committed to dealing with the lessathi?"

"Of course," I say, glancing at the others to ensure no one has had second thoughts.

"What about your companion?" Golmyck asks. "Will she be participating?"

"We haven't briefed her," Kate says, "since you asked to keep this discussion private, but given the circumstances, she will likely want to join."

"Indeed," Golmyck says. "Especially since the lessathi in question are the ones who imprisoned her and conspired to sell her father into slavery."

"What are you talking about?" Leila writes. "Why are you fighting the lessathi?"

"A select group of lessathi in this city acts as overseers for the other kings, keeping Golmyck in check," Kate explains. "We intend to remove them."

"You want to kill all the lessathi here?" Leila writes in shock. "If you kill any of them, word will reach their headquarters. You will become their prime targets!"

"I would be surprised if I were not already on their list," Kate replies. "They know who I am."

"They will not have time to alert their leadership," Golmyck assures us. "I accepted your help because a single strike can neutralize all four before they can send word."

"How so?" Hadrik asks.

"They are holding a meeting in two hours," Golmyck explains, "in a subterranean vault near this palace. They plan to discuss the political fallout of the earl of Ollendor's murder. The meeting was originally set for after your execution, but Eiden's intervention delayed it. With all four compelled to attend, you can strike the full enclave at once without any of them escaping into hiding."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Traitor, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Traitor)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Traitor
TEXT:

 "How do we get there undetected?" Daren asks.

"This room connects to an extensive network of underground tunnels," Golmyck says. "One corridor leads straight to their headquarters. My scouts trailed Barry there weeks ago. The lessathi don't know about this private entrance, so they haven't posted guards along it."

"Wait," Hadrik says. "You mean Barry your servant, right?"

"Yes, my servant!" Golmyck says with a chuckle. "I keep forgetting to specify."

"If it's your servant, why not just ask him directly instead of having him trailed?"

"Because my servant is an informant," Golmyck says with a smile. "He has worked with the lessathi for years. That is why he never enters this private chamber."

"An informant?" Hadrik asks, astonished. "Why keep him around if you know he's leaking information?"

"Because he isn't very clever," Golmyck says. "He is easy to read and never realizes when he is being followed. A predictable plant is far more useful than an operative smart enough to deceive me. By dropping harmless crumbs of information, I maintain an unwitting spy inside their network with minimal effort."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Map, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Map)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Map
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch2_tell_servant == 1) {
 So the king's servant was an informant... That explains why the lessathi in the holding cells knew of my stat device. I showed it to the servant on the way to the arena. Careless.

"Does that mean you intend to execute the servant once our task is complete?" Daren asks.

"Goodness, no!" Golmyck says. "Barry is harmless. There would be no justification for executing him. He knows no lessathi beyond this city's enclave. Once those four are removed, he returns to ordinary servant duties, minus the espionage."

"Do you possess a floor plan of the lower tunnels to guide us?" Kate asks.

"As a matter of fact, I do!" Golmyck draws a folded parchment from his pocket and spreads it across the desk.

He unrolls the schematic over the workbench, tracing the corridors in charcoal ink, pointing out our starting point and the exact vault where the four overseers meet.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_tell_servant == 0) {
 "Does that mean you intend to execute the servant once our task is complete?" Daren asks.

"Goodness, no!" Golmyck says. "Barry is harmless. There would be no justification for executing him. He knows no lessathi beyond this city's enclave. Once those four are removed, he returns to ordinary servant duties, minus the espionage."

"Do you possess a floor plan of the lower tunnels to guide us?" Kate asks.

"As a matter of fact, I do!" Golmyck draws a folded parchment from his pocket and spreads it across the desk.

He unrolls the schematic over the workbench, tracing the corridors in charcoal ink, pointing out our starting point and the exact vault where the four overseers meet.

}
 "Arraka, can you—" Illuna starts.

"Yes, yes, give me a moment," Arraka snaps from the amulet.

A glowing hologram of the lower network materializes in the air above the golden pendant. The projection differs from her usual maps: while most passages gleam in bright blue lines, several segments are sketched in emerald green.

"Why the different colors?" I ask, leaning over the light.

"The green corridors are blind to my magical sense," Arraka says. "I projected them only because they appear on the parchment. They are lined with seredium, which blocks my perception entirely. I cannot tell if they are occupied, collapsed, or barricaded. The primary route to their vault has no seredium plating, however, so at minimum you won't stumble into an ambush along that passage."

choice(""What about the meeting room? Is there anyone inside it right now?"", B2-Ch07a-Papers, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Papers, v_b2_ch7_tunnel = 0)
choice(""Can you sense any tunnels that are not on the king's map?"", B2-Ch07a-Papers, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Papers, v_b2_ch7_tunnel = 1)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Papers
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0) {
 "What about the meeting room? Is there anyone inside it right now?"

"No," Arraka says. "Their vault is completely empty. I would have marked living auras with dots."

"Where do we wait for the next two hours?" Daren asks. "Do we head back above?"

"No, absolutely not," Golmyck says quickly. "Departing now only to return shortly before their council would tip off my servant. You are welcome to wait here. I lack spare chairs, but the flagstones are clean if you wish to sit."

He presses his royal stamp onto two final parchments and passes them across the desk.

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1) {
 "Can you sense any tunnels that are not on the king's map?"

"Actually, yes," Arraka says. "A few. Let me project them."

Three additional blue conduits appear on the hovering hologram, branching off the charted paths.

"Look at this," I point to a side corridor. "This route connects our passage directly into one of the seredium-lined halls, which also leads toward their enclave."

"True, but I cannot verify if the seredium passage remains passable," Arraka warns. "I traced it from the royal parchment. It could be garrisoned or sealed for all I know."

"Where do we wait for the next two hours?" Daren asks. "Do we head back above?"

"No, absolutely not," Golmyck says quickly. "Departing now only to return shortly before their council would tip off my servant. You are welcome to wait here. I lack spare chairs, but the flagstones are clean if you wish to sit."

He presses his royal stamp onto two final parchments and passes them across the desk.

}
 "There you are," the king says. "These pardons absolve you of all charges across Varathia. Now, if you have no further requirements, I will resume repairs on the telepathic broadcaster meant to transmit tournament objectives. I have spent over a week trying to diagnose the malfunction, and the stubborn thing refuses to cooperate."

As Golmyck returns to his tools, Hadrik slides his rucksack to the floor and produces a deck of tavern cards.

"Well," Hadrik grins, shuffling the worn deck, "who is up for a game?"

We spend the next hour seated on the stones, playing a northern bluffing game. The traditional tavern rule required a sip of dwarven ale after every lost hand, but we omit the alcohol to keep our senses sharp. The rules reward deception, which makes Leila unbeatable thanks to her aura-reading. My spiky aura betrays every bluff I attempt, and after losing round after round, I set my cards aside to cross-reference my notes on Eiden's methods.

"Hey, Daren," I call over the table after reviewing my diagrams. "Think back to when Eiden paralyzed the three of you before teleporting us outside Thilias."

"What?" Daren glances over his cards. "I remember. What about it?"

"How many paralysis wards were you keeping active?"

"Just one," Daren says. "And my barrier has no paralysis component, so don't blame ward overload!"

"Understood," I say. "Is anyone else using a paralysis ward?"

"Yes," Kate says. "I cast the formula from Azarius's latest treatise."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Unconscious, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Unconscious)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Unconscious
TEXT:

 "And you, Daren?" I ask. "Which formula?"

"The golden one," Daren says. "The spinning sparkle matrix."

"Right, the standard white-mage formulation," I say. "And Hadrik, you rely on your natural giant constitution to blunt debilitating hexes?"

"Aye," Hadrik nods. "Yet I froze solid right alongside Kate and Daren."

"And do you know what those three defenses share?" I shut my notebook. "Nothing. Which means Eiden didn't exploit a warding loophole. He didn't cast paralysis at all. Remember when Kate's friend knocked us flat in the woods? That wasn't a sleep spell; she discharged lightning. Eiden used an electric current to lock your nervous systems. You felt an initial jolt before falling, followed by rhythmic shocks to keep your limbs immobilized."

"Now that you mention it, yes," Daren says, looking up from his cards. "There were distinct pulses. The numbness felt so similar to magical paralysis that I didn't question it. Does that mean Eiden wields lightning as a freeform element?"

"Doubtful," I say. "The construct had rigid mechanical constraints. It matches an ability from my stat device, so it's likely identical. It carries a once-a-day limit and a very narrow area of effect. Rolling a couple paces to the side pulls you out of range. It caught you because you stood shoulder to shoulder and didn't recognize the construct. If you know the timing, you can roll clear right before the next pulse hits, as the paralysis weakens briefly between discharges."

"Easier said than done," Daren mutters. "I fought against the hold the entire time."

"Straining against it only triggers faster pulses!" I say. "You have to stay relaxed and move at the final second. You track the rhythm over a couple shocks, find the pattern, and roll when the window opens. A dedicated lightning ward avoids the problem entirely, though keeping one active around the clock drains far too much energy."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Careful, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Careful)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Careful
TEXT:

 "Not to cut this short," Hadrik says, "but we should finish the round before we head out. We have barely half an hour before the lessathi convene, and everyone except Leila is holding at least six cards."

Once the round concludes, we leave our packs in Golmyck's care and prepare to descend into the lower tunnels.

"Stay vigilant," Golmyck warns from his workbench. "The lessathi lack casting ability, but their advanced artifacts make them as dangerous as any seasoned tournament contender. I know little of their individual arsenal, except that the operative wielding dual scythes utilizes electrical discharges. The capabilities of the other three remain unknown."

"At least we know who to target first," I say.

The gnome unlatches a stone trapdoor in the corner, and a folding brass ladder extends into the dark shaft below. We climb down one by one. Once we touch the tunnel floor, Golmyck wishes us fortune and retracts the ladder, sealing the hatch above with a solid thud. Looking up, the seam vanishes into the rough ceiling stone, undetectable unless you know the exact mechanism.

#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0) {
 We advance through the damp rock corridor, following the king's directions while checking with Arraka periodically for any signs of sentries.

"Look, their meeting has started!" Flower whispers, pointing at the glowing green dots shifting inside the vault on Arraka's hologram.

"A few minutes early," Daren observes, watching the map. "We will still reach them before they conclude. The final corridor is just ahead. These empty passages make me uneasy, though. It feels uncomfortably like a trap."

"Don't borrow trouble, Daren," Hadrik says. "The king confirmed the lessathi know nothing of his trapdoor. It makes sense they wouldn't post sentries in these abandoned branches. Perhaps they have guards at their vault door to settle your nerves."

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1) {
 We advance through the damp rock corridor, following the king's directions while checking with Arraka periodically for any signs of sentries.

"Look, their meeting has started!" Flower whispers, pointing at the glowing green dots shifting inside the vault on Arraka's hologram.

"A few minutes early," Daren observes, watching the map. "We will still reach them before they conclude. The final corridor is just ahead, and then—"

He halts, staring at the hologram with narrowed eyes.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Premonition, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Premonition) if (v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Interested, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Interested) if (v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Interested
TEXT:

 "Arraka," Daren says as we halt beside him, "this is where you detected the unmapped corridor, correct?"

"Right here," Arraka says. "There is likely a hidden latch in the rock face."

"And you believe this passage connects directly to the seredium tunnel leading to their enclave?" Daren asks.

"I told you," Arraka replies, "I cannot see inside. It could connect through, or it could terminate in a solid dead end. And even if it leads through, it might be packed with guards for all I can sense."

"Why the sudden interest in that passage, Daren?" Hadrik asks. "Why not stay on the charted path?"

"These empty tunnels feel wrong," Daren says, scanning the shadows. "Even assuming the lessathi guarded only the entrances they know about, finding zero resistance along the approach feels far too convenient."

choice(""I think you're worrying over nothing."", B2-Ch07a-Suspect, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Suspect)
choice(""I agree. What if they already know that the king's servant was being followed?"", B2-Ch07a-Relax, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Relax, v_b2_ch7_rock = 0)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Suspect
TEXT:

 "I think you're worrying over nothing."

"Agreed," Hadrik says. "They have no reason to suspect an assault from this angle. And if trouble arises, they rely on their artifacts for defense, so stationary guards wouldn't add much."

"Perhaps," Daren mutters, though he keeps his hand on his hilt.

"Come on," Hadrik says. "We're two minutes out. If they posted sentries outside the vault, you'll have your fight."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Premonition, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Premonition)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Premonition
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0 && v_premonition < 4 || v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1 && v_premonition < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_premonition == 4)
#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1 && v_premonition < 4) {
 

As we advance down the corridor, doubt creeps in over bypassing the secret side tunnel. The passage remains dead silent, and an uneasy chill settles over my shoulders as the destination nears. The thought barely takes shape before a deafening blast erupts beneath our boots. The ceiling caves in with crushing force, burying us in tons of shattered rock and killing me instantly.

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0 && v_premonition < 4) {
 

As we advance down the corridor, Daren's warning echoes in my mind. What if the route is compromised? What if the lessathi anticipated this approach? We should double back and seek an alternate path while we still can. The thought barely takes shape before a deafening blast erupts beneath our boots. The ceiling caves in with crushing force, burying us in tons of shattered rock and killing me instantly.

}
#if(v_premonition == 4) {
 

As we advance down the corridor, a violent vision flashes across my mind: our group stepping forward, triggering a catastrophic detonation that buries us under collapsing stone.

"Stop!" I shout, throwing an arm out.

Everyone freezes. "What is it?" Kate demands, frost already gathering at her fingertips.

"The corridor ahead is rigged to blow the moment we step on it," I say, heart hammering.

"A premonition from your device?" Kate asks.

"Yes. We cannot proceed this way. We have to turn back."

"Why rig this specific tunnel?" Hadrik asks, scratching his beard. "Isn't this the passage the servant uses to visit them? Why risk collapsing their own access route?"

"They know," Daren says grimly. "The listening devices in the throne room revealed our secret meetings with Golmyck. Even without finding the trapdoor, they had ample reason to secure this approach."

"Blowing an entire corridor on a suspicion seems extreme," Hadrik grunts. "Barry, are you certain your artifact isn't misreading the future? Do these visions always manifest?"

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_premonition < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_premonition < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_premonition < 4)
choice(""Well, why don't you throw a rock, and see for yourself if it explodes, then?"", B2-Ch07a-Secret, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Secret, v_b2_ch7_rock = 1) if (v_premonition == 4)
choice(""It's certainly reliable enough to not want to risk my life by ignoring it."", B2-Ch07a-Secret, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Secret, v_b2_ch7_rock = 0) if (v_premonition == 4)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Secret
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch7_rock == 1 && v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0) {
 "Well, why don't you throw a rock, and see for yourself if it explodes, then?"

"Fair enough!" Hadrik scoops a heavy stone from the ground and hurls it down the corridor.

The moment it strikes the flagstones, a massive explosion rips through the tunnel. Fire and thunder tear through the passage, bringing the ceiling down in an avalanche of boulders that chokes the corridor completely.

"Right," Hadrik coughs through the dust. "Point taken, Barry. Let's head back."

"The lessathi certainly heard that blast," Daren says, drawing his sword.

"If they heard it, they aren't reacting," I say, checking the floating map. "The four markers haven't moved an inch. Either their vault is soundproofed, or they assume we just died in the collapse. We need a way around this cave-in. Arraka, can you spot any unmapped side passages nearby?"

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_rock == 0 && v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0) {
 "It's certainly reliable enough to not want to risk my life by ignoring it."

"Fair enough," Hadrik says. "Which direction do we take if the king's path is impassable?"

"Arraka," I say, "do you sense any unmapped tunnels around here?"

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_rock == 1 && v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1) {
 "Well, why don't you throw a rock, and see for yourself if it explodes, then?"

"Fair enough!" Hadrik scoops a heavy stone from the ground and hurls it down the corridor.

The moment it strikes the flagstones, a massive explosion rips through the tunnel. Fire and thunder tear through the passage, bringing the ceiling down in an avalanche of boulders that chokes the corridor completely.

"Right," Hadrik coughs through the dust. "Point taken, Barry. Let's head back."

"The lessathi certainly heard that blast," Daren says, drawing his sword.

"If they heard it, they aren't reacting," I say, checking the floating map. "The four markers haven't moved an inch. Either their vault is soundproofed, or they assume we just died in the collapse."

"So we take the secret side passage from earlier?" Hadrik asks.

"We do," I say.

"Stand back, then," Hadrik says. "I'll clear the entrance."

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_rock == 0 && v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1) {
 "It's certainly reliable enough to not want to risk my life by ignoring it."

"Fair enough," Hadrik says. "So we take the secret side passage from earlier?"

"We do," I say.

"Stand back, then," Hadrik says. "I'll clear the entrance."

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 0) {
 "Hold on," Arraka says. "I do spot a few. Let me project them onto the map."

Three new blue lines sketch themselves across the hovering projection.

"There," I point to a side branch. "That corridor links our passage with the seredium-lined tunnel leading to their enclave."

"Again, I cannot guarantee the seredium tunnel is clear," Arraka reminds us. "I only know where the walls lie. It could be barricaded or guarded."

"Better than a dead end," I say. "Which wall conceals the entrance? That one?"

I point toward the right-hand rock face.

"That's the spot," Arraka confirms.

"Leave it to me," Hadrik says, stepping toward the rock.

"Wait," Daren raises a hand. "Now that we know the location, finding the concealed lever shouldn't take—"

Hadrik drives his fist through the solid masonry. Stone shatters with a resounding crack, crumbling inward to reveal a hollow passage.

Daren presses his palm against his face with a groan. "Must you do that every single time?"

"Relax!" Hadrik brushes rubble from his knuckles. "The lessathi are too far to hear crumbling stone, and if sentries were waiting on the other side, sneaking past in a single-file tunnel was never an option. Direct path to their headquarters. Moving on."

"Fine," Daren sighs. "Let us proceed."

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_tunnel == 1) {
 "Wait," Daren raises a hand. "Now that we know the location, finding the concealed lever shouldn't take—"

Hadrik drives his fist through the solid masonry. Stone shatters with a resounding crack, crumbling inward to reveal a hollow passage.

Daren presses his palm against his face with a groan. "Must you do that every single time?"

"Relax!" Hadrik brushes rubble from his knuckles. "The lessathi are too far to hear crumbling stone, and if sentries were waiting on the other side, sneaking past in a single-file tunnel was never an option. Direct path to their headquarters. Moving on."

"Fine," Daren sighs. "Let us proceed."

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Hearing, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Hearing)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Relax
TEXT:

 "I agree. What if they already know that the king's servant was being followed?"

"You think this is an ambush?" Hadrik asks.

"It is entirely possible," Daren says. "The lessathi maintain their own network of spies, and their listening devices in the throne room revealed our private meetings with Golmyck. Even without discovering the trapdoor, leaving themselves completely exposed during this gathering would be reckless."

"As long as the alternate route reaches the destination, I support changing corridors," Kate says.

"If everyone agrees, I will open the way," Hadrik says, stepping toward the wall.

"Wait," Daren says. "Now that we know the location, finding the concealed lever shouldn't take—"

Hadrik drives his fist through the solid masonry. Stone shatters with a resounding crack, crumbling inward to reveal a hollow passage.

Daren presses his palm against his face with a groan. "Must you do that every single time?"

"Relax!" Hadrik brushes rubble from his knuckles. "The lessathi are too far to hear us, and if sentries were waiting on the other side, sneaking past in a single-file tunnel was never an option. Direct path to their headquarters. Moving on."

"Fine," Daren sighs. "We will find out soon enough if this detour was wise."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Hearing, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Hearing)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Hearing
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch7_culprit,1) if (v_ancient_languages >= 3 && v_hearing >= 2)
set(v_b2_ch7_overheard,0) if (v_ancient_languages < 3 || v_hearing < 2)
set(v_b2_ch7_overheard,1) if (v_ancient_languages >= 3 && v_hearing >= 2)
achievement("Found the culprit",v_ac_b2_ch7_culprit)
#if(v_hearing < 2) {
 

We traverse the unmapped tunnel without meeting resistance. At the far end, Hadrik checks our positions and shatters the thin rock partition with a single blow, clearing the threshold into the seredium-plated corridor. The hall stretches ahead, grey and silent.

"Arraka," Illuna murmurs, "do you sense guards?"

"Nothing," Arraka replies. "The passage is clear of arcane signatures and magical traps. Mechanical triggers are on you."

"Pressure plates trigger under foot," Hadrik says, scooping a handful of gravel. "I will toss stones ahead and take point. Giant hide can weather a blast if something clicks."

"Keep your auras dampened," Daren whispers as we move forward. "We cannot afford to announce our approach."

A minute of cautious pacing brings us to a junction where the primary tunnel and our bypass converge. A narrow passage branches left, terminating at a heavy iron-banded door. Beyond the wood, muted voices indicate the council is underway.

"Barry," Daren whispers, gesturing from the shadows. "Over here."

I slip into the narrow corridor beside the others, weapons drawn, waiting for Daren's signal to breach.

}
#if(v_hearing >= 2 && v_ancient_languages < 3) {
 

We traverse the unmapped tunnel without meeting resistance. At the far end, Hadrik checks our positions and shatters the thin rock partition with a single blow, clearing the threshold into the seredium-plated corridor. The hall stretches ahead, grey and silent.

"Arraka," Illuna murmurs, "do you sense guards?"

"Nothing," Arraka replies. "The passage is clear of arcane signatures and magical traps. Mechanical triggers are on you."

"Pressure plates trigger under foot," Hadrik says, scooping a handful of gravel. "I will toss stones ahead and take point. Giant hide can weather a blast if something clicks."

"Keep your auras dampened," Daren whispers as we move forward. "We cannot afford to announce our approach."

Faint voices drift from the far end of the hall. The cadence matches the measured, soft-spoken tone of the operative who visited my cell below the arena. Other voices answer, though the words are spoken in rapid, sharp Lessathi syllables that slip past my understanding.

A minute of cautious pacing brings us to a junction where the primary tunnel and our bypass converge. A narrow passage branches left, terminating at a heavy iron-banded door. Beyond the wood, muted voices indicate the council is underway.

"Barry," Daren whispers, gesturing from the shadows. "Over here."

I slip into the narrow corridor beside the others, weapons drawn, waiting for Daren's signal to breach.

}
#if(v_ancient_languages >= 3 && v_hearing >= 2) {
 

We traverse the unmapped tunnel without meeting resistance. At the far end, Hadrik checks our positions and shatters the thin rock partition with a single blow, clearing the threshold into the seredium-plated corridor. The hall stretches ahead, grey and silent.

"Arraka," Illuna murmurs, "do you sense guards?"

"Nothing," Arraka replies. "The passage is clear of arcane signatures and magical traps. Mechanical triggers are on you."

"Pressure plates trigger under foot," Hadrik says, scooping a handful of gravel. "I will toss stones ahead and take point. Giant hide can weather a blast if something clicks."

"Keep your auras dampened," Daren whispers as we move forward. "We cannot afford to announce our approach."

Faint voices carry clearly down the stone passage. I recognize the calm cadence of the operative who visited my cell beneath the sands, speaking in formal Lessathi.

"It remains our only viable course," he says. "Ollendor is already isolated from the eastern courts. The other crowns will not intervene if Thilias severs diplomatic ties. The gnome king will enact the embargo regardless, leaving no cause for us to interfere."

"Ollendor is a minor distraction!" another operative snaps. "Do you realize how many foreign mages have perished since the opening bell? This is precisely why I demanded a tournament charter barring lethal duels outside formal trials!"

"We settled this," the soft-spoken operative replies smoothly. "The royal courts refused. They deemed bloodshed an integral Varathian custom, even among foreign contestants."

"Curse the kings and their barbarism!" the second voice snarls. "They ruined the timeline! Why did I risk sabotaging the telepathic broadcaster to delay the first round if the contestants were simply going to slaughter each other in the alleys anyway?"

"You repeat this complaint at every gathering," a third voice cuts in weary. "What is done is done. Focus on the current disposition."

"Barry," Daren whispers from ahead. "Over here."

While tracking the argument, our line has reached the final junction. The passages reunite before a narrow corridor sealed by a reinforced oak door. On the other side, the overseers continue their debate, oblivious to our presence.

I move into position beside Daren, dagger in hand, waiting for his breach command.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Welcome, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Welcome)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Welcome
TEXT:

#if(v_ancient_languages < 3) {
 

As we tense to kick the door open, an electric pulse rips through the stone beneath our boots. The shock seizes my spine, locking my muscles instantly. My knees give out, dropping me hard onto the flagstones. Beside me, Daren, Kate, Hadrik, Leila, and Flower hit the ground in identical paralysis.

The electric pulse... Eiden's trap.

The heavy door swings outward. Four figures in dark blue hooded robes file into the narrow hallway, weapons held at the ready.

"Welcome, travelers," the soft-spoken lessathi from my cell says in Common. "Some of us have already been introduced; others have not. It makes little difference. We will ask the questions, and you will provide the answers. Is that understood?"

One of his comrades mutters a sharp response in Lessathi.

"Where are your manners?" the first operative chides in Common. "These are guests. Speak the Common tongue so they may follow the proceedings."

The second operative ignores the reprimand, snapping another reply in their native dialect.

"Suit yourself," the soft-spoken one sighs. "A single interrogator suffices."

}
#if(v_ancient_languages >= 3) {
 

As we tense to kick the door open, an electric pulse rips through the stone beneath our boots. The shock seizes my spine, locking my muscles instantly. My knees give out, dropping me hard onto the flagstones. Beside me, Daren, Kate, Hadrik, Leila, and Flower hit the ground in identical paralysis.

The electric pulse... Eiden's trap.

The heavy door swings outward. Four figures in dark blue hooded robes file into the narrow hallway, weapons held at the ready.

"Welcome, travelers," the soft-spoken lessathi from my cell says in Common. "Some of us have already been introduced; others have not. It makes little difference. We will ask the questions, and you will provide the answers. Is that understood?"

"They cannot answer, fool," another operative says in Lessathi. "The current locks the vocal cords entirely."

"Where are your manners?" the first operative chides in Common. "These are guests. Speak the Common tongue so they may follow the proceedings."

"Is this your idea of wit?" the second replies in Lessathi. "Your humor was always tedious."

"Suit yourself," the soft-spoken one sighs. "A single interrogator suffices."

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Narrow, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Narrow)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Narrow
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch7_rock == 0) {
 "I told you this would happen," a third operative says in Common. "That royal lackey never notices when he is trailed."

"Indeed," the soft-spoken leader replies. "Leaking our council time to the servant proved an effective lure. What puzzles me is how they bypassed the demolition trap in the main corridor. Did the gnome provide an unmapped architectural schematic?"

"It matters little," the second operative says. "Extract the intelligence and dispose of them. The two with lessathi blood should retain enough motor control to speak under the dampener. Question them quickly."

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_rock == 1) {
 "I told you this would happen," a third operative says in Common. "That royal lackey never notices when he is trailed."

"Indeed," the soft-spoken leader replies. "Leaking our council time to the servant proved an effective lure. What puzzles me is how they survived the blast in the main corridor. Did they detect the trigger and deploy a decoy?"

"It matters little," the second operative says. "Extract the intelligence and dispose of them. The two with lessathi blood should retain enough motor control to speak under the dampener. Question them quickly."

}
 They deployed the exact electric trap Eiden used. In this cramped hall, the pulse blankets the entire floor. But my lessathi bloodline grants a partial electrical resistance, blunting the lock between pulses. Leila has the same advantage. Daren, Kate, and Hadrik will need several cycles to read the discharge rhythm.

As I lie on the cold stone, glowing blue script floats inches before my face.

"Don't free yourself yet," Leila's message reads. "Wait for the others to gauge the discharge intervals. I am messaging everyone. When I give the signal, we break together."

choice("Attack the first lessathi that gets close to me.", B2-Ch07a-Amulet, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Amulet, v_b2_ch7_wait = 0)
choice("Wait for Leila's signal.", B2-Ch07a-Amulet, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Amulet, v_b2_ch7_wait = 1)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Amulet
TEXT:

 "Where did you hide the casting matrix?" Arraka's voice screeches from the amulet. "I have scoured this corridor since you opened that door! There is no magical emitter here!"

Whether she is buying us time or furious that non-magical technology eludes her senses is anyone's guess. Likely the latter.

"It would make a poor trap if a spirit could spot it from ten paces," the soft-spoken leader says mildly.

"Who is speaking?" the third operative asks, hand dropping to his weapon. "Where is that voice coming from?"

"The banshee bound within the pendant," the leader replies. "Arraka, if reports from twenty years ago hold true. But the banshee is of no consequence."

He steps across the threshold into the active field, unaffected by the current. Insulated boots or an internal dampener.

"You are the one I want," he says, stopping two paces from me. "I did not anticipate your survival in the arena, fellow lessathi. Tenacious. Tell me, did Golmyck provide the tunnel layouts? How did you evade the demolition charge?"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Attack, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Attack) if (v_b2_ch7_wait == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Wait, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Wait) if (v_b2_ch7_wait == 1)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Attack
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility >= 3 || v_combat_technique >= 3 || v_strength >= 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 3 && v_combat_technique < 3 && v_strength < 3)
#if(v_strength >= 3) {
 

While he speaks, I count the interval between pulses.

Two seconds before the next discharge, I push off the floor and drive my shoulder forward, clearing the field. My hands clamp around his collar before he can raise his blade. With a single heave, I lift him off his feet and slam him skull-first into the stone wall. The impact cracks masonry, and he collapses limp to the floor.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 3 && v_strength < 3) {
 

While he speaks, I count the interval between pulses.

Two seconds before the next discharge, I roll clear of the field and sweep upward. My left hand catches his wrist, twisting his arm behind his shoulder and wrenching his dagger free. In one continuous motion, I drive his own blade across his throat. He clutches at his neck, blood spilling through his fingers, before collapsing against the stones.

}
#if(v_agility >= 3 && v_combat_technique < 3 && v_strength < 3) {
 

While he speaks, I count the interval between pulses.

Two seconds before the next discharge, I vault to my feet, clearing the trap's perimeter. My dagger clears its sheath in a flash of steel, slicing cleanly across his exposed throat before his guard can rise. He stumbles back against the wall, hands pressed to the wound, and slumps to the floor.

}
#if(v_agility < 3 && v_combat_technique < 3 && v_strength < 3) {
 

While he speaks, I count the interval between pulses.

Two seconds before the next discharge, I lurch to my feet and thrust my dagger toward his throat. The operative reads the clumsy lunge, pivoting smoothly out of the arc. As I overextend, he whips his blade through the air. The swipe isn't aimed to cut—a pressurized spray of caustic acid shoots from the hilt directly into my eyes.

The burning fluid melts flesh and bone in a flare of agony. Before I can raise a guard, his dagger drives hard into my throat, ending the fight.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Trident, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Trident) if (v_agility >= 3 || v_combat_technique >= 3 || v_strength >= 3)
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_agility < 3 && v_combat_technique < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_agility < 3 && v_combat_technique < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_agility < 3 && v_combat_technique < 3 && v_strength < 3)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Wait
TEXT:

 "An interrogation requires only one subject," the operative wielding dual scythes says, breaking his silence.

He steps over the floor toward Leila, who lies prone against the stone.

"What are you doing?" the soft-spoken leader snaps, turning from me. "We need both intact!"

"Do we?" The scythes wielder catches a fistful of Leila's silver hair, yanking her head back so she is forced to look up at him. "I have waited years to finish this reject. I will not hold back any longer."

choice("Try to distract the lessathi by telling him about Eiden's message.", B2-Ch07a-Winter, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Winter)
choice("Wait for Leila's signal.", B2-Ch07a-Wait2, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Wait2)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Wait2
TEXT:

 "Stand down!" the leader commands. "Control yourself!"

"Control myself?" the scythes wielder snarls. "You were not stationed at the Beacon. Living alongside this defective creature was nauseating. And that traitorous caretaker treated her as an equal. Disgusting."

He glares down at Leila as her silver eyes harden.

"Angry on behalf of your dear father?" the operative sneers. "He got off lightly. Slaves of his sort should be grateful for scraps. You freed him for a few weeks, but we will drag him back to the pens. And when we do, he will receive the end he earned: discarded with the rest of the refuse."

Rage erupts behind Leila's eyes. Dropping all restraint, she lunges upward from the floor, driving both knives upward into his chest.

I vault clear of the field simultaneously, catching the soft-spoken leader off guard while his back is turned. My dagger sweeps across his exposed neck in a single stroke before he can pivot.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Trident, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Trident)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Trident
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch7_cookie,1) if (v_toughness == 4)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_toughness < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b2_ch7_wait == 0 && v_toughness == 4 || v_b2_ch7_wait == 1 && v_toughness == 4)
achievement("One tough cookie",v_ac_b2_ch7_cookie)
#if(v_toughness < 4) {
 

"Die!" the third operative barks, driving a three-pronged steel trident into the masonry.

A massive fist of solid rock tears through the wall behind me, clamping around my torso with crushing force.

I struggle to draw breath, but stone fingers lock my ribs tight. The fist contracts, shattering bone and tearing internal organs, killing me before I can scream.

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_wait == 0 && v_toughness == 4) {
 

"Die!" the third operative barks, driving a three-pronged steel trident into the masonry.

A massive fist of solid rock tears through the wall behind me, clamping around my torso with crushing force.

I strain against the grip, but my arms are pinned to my sides. My augmented toughness bears the brunt of the pressure, keeping my ribs from caving inward under the stone vise.

Before the operative can tighten his grip, Leila springs from the floor. Her dagger sinks into the side of his skull, dropping him instantly. As the stone hand crumbles into dust, Kate breaks clear of the electric field, leaping backward into the corridor. She thrusts an open palm toward the scythes wielder, sending an icicle through his forehead before he can raise a guard.

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_wait == 1 && v_toughness == 4) {
 

"Die!" the third operative barks, driving a three-pronged steel trident into the masonry.

A massive fist of solid rock tears through the wall behind me, clamping around my torso with crushing force.

I strain against the grip, but my arms are pinned to my sides. My augmented toughness bears the brunt of the pressure, keeping my ribs from caving inward under the stone vise.

Kate breaks clear of the electric field with a backward leap. Extending a palm toward the trident wielder, she launches a jagged ice spike straight through his forehead. The stone fist dissolves into grey powder the moment he hits the floor.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_toughness < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_toughness < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_toughness < 4)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Blinded, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Blinded) if (v_toughness == 4)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Winter
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch7_delivered,1)
achievement("Message delivered",v_ac_b2_ch7_delivered)
 "Hey!" I shout. "Eiden gave me a message for your enclave. He said to remember the still winter."

The scythes wielder freezes. His fingers loosen in Leila's hair, and he turns toward me, fear cutting through his arrogance.

"What did you say?"

"Ignore him," the leader orders, stepping closer. "He is baiting you."

"Ignore him?" the scythes wielder snarls, turning on his superior. "You want me to stand down while a stillwater's messenger mocks us?"

"I want you to exercise discipline—"

"Now!" Leila's blue lettering blazes before my eyes.

I vault upward, clearing the edge of the discharge field with my blade leveled at the leader's throat. His back is turned, and my edge cuts deep across his neck before he can react. Simultaneously, Leila lunges from the stone, driving her knife to the hilt in the scythes wielder's chest.

A second later, Kate rolls clear of the field, thrusting an open hand toward the operative with the trident. An ice cone hammers through his skull, pinning him to the far wall. Daren, Hadrik, and Flower remain prone on the floor, still working through the shock intervals.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Blinded, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Blinded)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Blinded
TEXT:

 The final operative raises an emerald-encrusted buckler. A searing flash of white light floods the passage, burning my vision white.

Blinking away the glare, I spot Leila and the operative disarmed against the far wall. Leila sits slumped against the stone, breathing hard, while the operative stoops to retrieve one of her fallen daggers.

"Help me, Barry!" large blue script flashes frantically in the air.

choice("Kill the lessathi.", B2-Ch07a-Kill, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Kill)
choice("Let her handle it.", B2-Ch07a-Handle, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Handle)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Kill
TEXT:

 I sprint forward, gripping my hilt with both hands, and bury the steel between his shoulder blades.

As I pull the blade back, the figure flickers. The operative dissolves into thin air, leaving Leila slumped against the stones, blood spreading across her chest. Across the corridor, the woman against the wall shimmers into the fourth operative, grinning viciously.

An illusion.

I drop to my knees, pressing my hands over Leila's wound. Her eyes are glassy, her chest still. Down the hall, Kate freezes in horror.

Before I can turn, the operative sweeps Leila's fallen dagger across my throat. Darkness closes in.

choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Handle
TEXT:

 Something feels wrong about the scene. I hold my ground, watching the spacing.

"Barry, please!" the text pleads again as the operative stumbles toward her, blinking through the residual flash.

I step forward to restrain him—

Three ice cones slam into the figure against the wall. A shriek of agony rips through the corridor.

A scream? Leila is mute.

The illusion dissolves. The figure on the stones shifts into the wounded operative, clutching bleeding puncture wounds in his side. The figure before me shimmers into Leila, poised with her second knife ready.

Kate wastes no time. A crystalline ice dagger flies from her fingers, striking the operative between the eyes.

She lowers her hand and gives me a sharp look.

"'Help me, Barry'?" Kate crosses her arms. "When has Leila ever played the helpless maiden? Especially against an amateur like this?"

"Did you deduce the disguise entirely from the phrasing?" I ask.

"Of course," Kate says.

"What if you had guessed wrong?"

"Daren would have had to expend a healing spell," Kate replies without missing a beat. "I placed the cones in non-vital tissue. No permanent harm."

I stare at her. "I don't know what to say to that."

"Deliver a quip, as usual," Kate says.

She turns toward the hall as Daren and Hadrik finally shake off the residual current.

"Search the vault," Kate says, heading through the doorway. "Perhaps they left records concerning Diane."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Precautionary, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Precautionary)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Precautionary
TEXT:

 "That was entirely too close," Daren mutters, rubbing his forearms as we enter the enclave. "We need a countermeasure against lightning."

"Aye," Hadrik grunts. "I haven't felt that helpless since Kate's friend blasted us in the clearing. If Barry hadn't timed the pulses, we'd be corpses."

"Fortunate that someone spent his youth reading in libraries," I say. "Right, Daren?"

"Quite," Daren grunts, pulling open the nearest desk drawer.

A thorough search yields nothing. Every compartment, shelf, and cabinet sits bare.

"Not a single parchment," Daren sighs. "Did they purge the vault in advance, anticipating an assault?"

"More likely when the servant was first suspected," I say. "Once a location is marked as compromised, lessathi clear out operational records immediately."

"Then we have nothing more to gain here," Kate says quietly. "No trace of Diane. Let us return."

"You could have kept the illusionist breathing for questioning," I tell Kate as we head for the door. "He was pinned by the first barrage. Minimal threat."

"Illusionists are never minimal threats," Kate replies. "Leaving an active weaver alive in a confined space is reckless."

"Do we claim their gear?" Hadrik asks, nodding at the fallen weapons.

"Without question," I say. "I'll take the buckler."

I lift the emerald-inlaid shield, turning it over to inspect the fittings. No runes, no trigger studs.

"No incantation was spoken when he cast the blinding flash or the disguise," I note. "There must be an internal conduit."

"Bring them to Golmyck," Daren suggests. "He understands device mechanics."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Climb, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Climb)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Climb
TEXT:

 "Hold on!" Hadrik jumps back a pace. "The electric field."

"Relax," I say, stepping across the threshold. "The discharge loop resets once the target zone clears."

I turn around in the empty corridor to demonstrate.

"Safe. Let's move."

We gather the lessathi artifacts and retrace our steps through the tunnels. Reaching the shaft beneath the royal basement, Hadrik tosses several pebbles against the overhead trapdoor. The latch clicks, and the brass ladder extends downward.

"Carrying these weapons up the rungs will be awkward," Daren says, looking at the bundle.

"Can you lash them to your shield harness?" I ask.

"The harness is tailored for a single shield," Daren says. "These polearms have no straps."

"You overthink everything," Hadrik says, snatching the trident. "Stand back."

He cups a hand around his mouth, shouting upward through the shaft.

"Golmyck! Catch incoming! Sharp edges!"

A small hand signals down from the hatch, and Hadrik heaves the weapons up one by one. Once the haul is clear, we scale the ladder, and the stone trapdoor thuds shut behind us.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Volunteered, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Volunteered)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Volunteered
TEXT:

 "Am I to assume the enclave has been eliminated?" Golmyck asks, stepping forward from his desk.

"All four," I confirm.

"Remarkable," Golmyck murmurs, looking us over. "And without an injury among you. You have my gratitude."

"Ensure the agreement holds," Daren says firmly. "We expect the slave auctions ended when next we pass through Thilias."

"Without fail," Golmyck promises. "The edicts for emancipation will be drafted by dawn. I regret that I cannot offer official compensation from the royal treasury. The clandestine nature of the enterprise prevents filing a formal disbursement."

"Unnecessary," I say. "We offered our blades freely. Had we sought bounties, we would have named a price."

"Even so, you should not depart unrewarded," Golmyck says. "Wait a moment. I have something of practical use."

He ducks beneath his workbench, re-emerging with a palm-sized brass housing fitted with a glass lens and a single toggle.

"This sensor identifies lessathi lineage," Golmyck explains, offering it forward. "Direct the lens at a subject and depress the toggle; the display registers their bloodline. I built it decades ago, before I learned to parse the finer nuances of mortal auras. It has gathered dust on my shelf, and it may serve you well."

choice("Take the device.", B2-Ch07a-Tailored, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Tailored, v_b2_ch7_reward = 1)
choice("Refuse the king's offer.", B2-Ch07a-Tailored, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Tailored, v_b2_ch7_reward = 0)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Tailored
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch7_average,1) if (v_available_points == 22)
achievement("Just an average assassin",v_ac_b2_ch7_average)
#if(v_b2_ch7_overheard == 1 && v_b2_ch7_reward == 1) {
 "We will take it," I say, pocketing the sensor. "Any tool that sharpens our awareness is welcome."

"What of the weaponry Hadrik tossed into your study?" Daren asks.

"Let me examine them," Golmyck says, turning to the pile on the floor.

"I tried activating the buckler," I say, "but found no trigger mechanism."

"Expected," Golmyck replies, turning the emerald shield in his hands. "These artifacts are keyed strictly to the unique aura signature of their designated wielder. Without matching their specific energetic frequency, the conduits remain inert. A precaution to keep their technology out of enemy hands."

"Completely useless to us, then?" I ask.

"As weapons, yes," Golmyck says. "Though disassembled, the internal components will prove invaluable for my other projects."

"On that subject," I say, "I overheard the overseers discussing your telepathic broadcaster before we breached the door. They intentionally sabotaged the relay to delay the opening round. They required time to execute a private operation before the first trial, but higher casualty rates among the mages derailed their timeline."

"A deliberate sabotage..." Golmyck muses, eyes lighting up. "I recall them petitioning the other courts to ban lethal combat outside scheduled trials. That explains the erratic feedback loop in the receiver. This narrows the repair significantly. My thanks."

"You caught their council from down the corridor?" Daren asks, glancing at me.

"Acoustic enhancement from my stat device," I say offhandedly. "We should collect our packs. The hour is late, and a feast awaits."

}
#if(v_b2_ch7_overheard == 1 && v_b2_ch7_reward == 0) {
 "Keep it," I say. "Two members of our company can already distinguish lessathi auras on sight. We have little need for the artifact."

"As you wish," Golmyck sets the device on his bench.

