}
 "A word of caution," Golmyck adds as we shoulder our gear. "Breathe no word of this strike beyond these walls. The cell is gone, but their informants remain scattered across Thilias. Many will disperse once payments cease, but loyalists may seek retribution. My own agents will root them out in time, but remain watchful."

"We will keep our guards up," Daren promises.

"Safe journeys," Golmyck bows. "The gates of Thilias remain open to you always."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Mansion, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Mansion)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Mansion
TEXT:

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0 && v_ch11_saved_slave == 3) {
 We shoulder our rucksacks, bid the king farewell, and climb back to the throne room. The servant watches us emerge with guarded eyes after two long hours below, but says nothing as he escorts us to the palace gates.

An hour and a half later, we reach the estate where Enrique paces the terrace.

"At last!" Enrique calls out. "I began to fear you had been delayed indefinitely!"

"Our apologies," Daren says. "Audience with the crown ran longer than planned."

"No matter, you are here," Enrique beams. "The kitchen stands ready. I will have the platters served immediately."

Minutes later, Enrique returns followed by five estate cooks bearing steaming platters of roasted meats, spiced tubers, and glazed pastries. The rich aromas easily rival the best of Flower's conjured dishes. Rose's younger siblings join us at the courtyard table, and we settle into the long-awaited dinner.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0 && v_ch11_saved_slave != 3) {
 We shoulder our rucksacks, bid the king farewell, and climb back to the throne room. The servant watches us emerge with guarded eyes after two long hours below, but says nothing as he escorts us to the palace gates.

An hour and a half later, we reach the estate where Enrique paces the terrace.

"At last!" Enrique calls out. "I began to fear you had been delayed indefinitely!"

"Our apologies," Daren says. "Audience with the crown ran longer than planned."

"No matter, you are here," Enrique beams. "The kitchen stands ready. I will have the platters served immediately."

Minutes later, Enrique returns followed by five estate cooks bearing steaming platters of roasted meats, spiced tubers, and glazed pastries. The rich aromas easily rival the best of Flower's conjured dishes. Ella and Rose's younger siblings join us at the courtyard table, and we settle into the long-awaited dinner.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1 && v_ch11_saved_slave == 3) {
 We shoulder our rucksacks, bid the king farewell, and climb back to the throne room. The servant watches us emerge with guarded eyes after two long hours below, but says nothing as he escorts us to the palace gates.

An hour and a half later, we reach the estate where Rose waits by the garden gate.

"At last!" Rose breathes a sigh of relief. "I was on the verge of calling the transceiver to confirm you were safe."

"Apologies," Daren says. "Business with the king took longer than anticipated."

"No need to apologize," Rose smiles warmly. "The dishes need a quick reheating, and we can sit down together in twenty minutes."

True to her word, Rose emerges with two laden trays. I step over to take one from her hands, helping arrange the dishes along the wide wooden bench. Her younger siblings run in from the yard, and we head back to the kitchen to carry the remaining courses out.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1 && v_ch11_saved_slave != 3) {
 We shoulder our rucksacks, bid the king farewell, and climb back to the throne room. The servant watches us emerge with guarded eyes after two long hours below, but says nothing as he escorts us to the palace gates.

An hour and a half later, we reach the estate where Rose waits by the garden gate.

"At last!" Rose breathes a sigh of relief. "I was on the verge of calling the transceiver to confirm you were safe."

"Apologies," Daren says. "Business with the king took longer than anticipated."

"No need to apologize," Rose smiles warmly. "The dishes need a quick reheating, and we can sit down together in twenty minutes."

True to her word, Rose emerges with two laden trays. I step over to take one from her hands, helping arrange the dishes along the wide wooden bench. Ella and Rose's younger siblings join us, and Ella helps carry the remaining courses out from the hearth.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
 We pass the following hours eating, drinking, and celebrating our survival and liberation from the arena.

The spreads prepared by the estate cooks prove exceptional, offering a variety of regional dishes none of us had encountered before. The cooks initially stood in a formal line beside the terrace, but an hour of Hadrik's persistent toasts wore down their reserve, and they were soon sharing flagons of dwarven ale alongside us. Before we retired, Enrique distributed packets of Rose's dried leaves to ensure clear heads at dawn.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
 We pass the following hours eating, drinking, and celebrating our survival and liberation from the arena.

Rose's cooking provides a welcome comfort, complemented by the delicacies Flower conjures with cheerful enthusiasm. Hadrik keeps the tankards filled with northern ale, and Rose distributes packets of her dried leaves before nightfall to guarantee clear heads at dawn.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Ending, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Ending)


