choice("Continue", B2-Ch07a-Ending, v_current_scene = B2-Ch07a-Ending)


ID: B2-Ch07a-Ending
TEXT:

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
 With a march set before sunrise, we bring the gathering to a close early to secure a few hours of rest, though the quiet evening was precisely what we needed after the strain of the coliseum.

Before first light, we assemble in the courtyard to bid Enrique farewell.

"Our acquaintance spanned barely a few days," Enrique says, bowing with theatrical flair, "yet they were memorable hours. I wish you all triumph, whether in claiming the Magium or whatever prize your hearts pursue."

"Farewell, Enrique," Daren says, clasping his forearm. "Keep the transceiver on your person. We may need to coordinate while the tournament unfolds."

We wave our goodbyes and navigate the darkened avenues toward the northern gate. After a few wrong turns through the upper tier, we reach the fortified archway just as the dawn breaks across the horizon. Melindra stands waiting by the stone pillar, leaning casually against the masonry.

She catches sight of us and waves. We quicken our pace, ready to resume the path we came to walk. The Magium awaits.

}
#if(v_ch11_romance_rose == 0 && v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
 With a march set before sunrise, we bring the gathering to a close early to secure a few hours of rest, though the quiet evening was precisely what we needed after the strain of the coliseum.

Before first light, we assemble in the courtyard to bid Rose farewell.

"Travel safely, Rose," Kate says, stepping back from an embrace. "I will not forget you."

"You speak as though we shall never meet again," Rose smiles gently. "You have no intention of dying out there, do you? Stay alive, and our paths will cross. Besides, you carry transceivers. A call reaches me anytime. It will be as though I never left."

"I... suppose you are right," Kate concedes.

}
#if(v_ch11_romance_rose == 1 && v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
 With a march set before sunrise, we bring the gathering to a close early to secure a few hours of rest, though the quiet evening was precisely what we needed after the strain of the coliseum.

Before first light, we assemble in the courtyard to bid Rose farewell.

"Travel safely, Rose," Kate says, stepping back from an embrace. "I will not forget you."

"You speak as though we shall never meet again," Rose smiles gently. "You have no intention of dying out there, do you? Stay alive, and our paths will cross. Besides, you carry transceivers. A call reaches me anytime. It will be as though I never left."

"I... suppose you are right," Kate concedes.

"Besides," Rose adds with a sly glance in my direction, "Barry promised to return for me the moment he claims the Magium. If you travel together, we will see each other before long."

Hadrik lets out a booming laugh.

"If Barry gave his word, it must be carved in stone!"

"Shut up," I mutter.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
 We wave our farewells to Rose and make our way toward the northern gate. After navigating the morning streets, we reach the outer portcullis just as the sun clears the wall. Melindra is already there, leaning back against the stone with arms folded.

She waves as we approach, and we pick up our pace, stepping forward into the road ahead. The Magium awaits.

}
